---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import {
  ChatInputAttachments,
  ChatInputComposer,
  ChatInputIntegrations,
  ChatInputStreaming,
} from '../../components/ChatInputDemo';
---

<Docs
  title="Chat Input"
  description="A rich chat message box with @ agents, / skills, # files, and model and project pickers."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Chat Input</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    The message box of a chat. Type <code>@</code> to tag an agent, <code>/</code>
    to add a skill, or <code>#</code> to add a file. Markdown and shortcuts format text. The bar holds attach and mode
    menus, a project picker, a model picker, and send.
  </p>
  <section class="prose-section" id="chat-input-composer">
    <h2 class="section-title">Chat input</h2>
    <ChatInputComposer client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="chat-input-integrations">
    <h2 class="section-title">Integrations</h2>
    <ChatInputIntegrations client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="chat-input-attachments">
    <h2 class="section-title">With attachments</h2>
    <ChatInputAttachments client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="chat-input-streaming">
    <h2 class="section-title">Working</h2>
    <ChatInputStreaming client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Chat input usage"
      code={`import { ChatInput } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/chat-input";

<ChatInput
  value={value}
  onValueChange={setValue}
  onSend={send}
  onStop={stop}
  status={streaming ? "streaming" : "idle"}
  agents={(query) => searchAgents(query)}
  skills={(query) => searchSkills(query)}
  files={(query) => searchFiles(query)}
  attachments={attachments}
  onRemoveAttachment={remove}
  attachActions={[{ id: "computer", label: "Upload from computer", onSelect: pickFiles }]}
  modes={[
    { id: "plan", label: "Plan", color: "#3b9ef5" },
    { id: "research", label: "Deep research", color: "#6366f1" },
  ]}
  mode={mode}
  onModeChange={setMode}
  projects={projects}
  project={project}
  onProjectChange={setProject}
  models={[{ id: "opus", label: "Claude Opus 5.5", brand: "claude" }]}
  model={model}
  onModelChange={setModel}
  prompts={[{ id: "clarify", label: "Clarify user problem" }]}
  integrations={[
    {
      id: "slack",
      label: "Slack",
      icon: <BrandIcon brand="slack" size="inline" />,
      accounts: [{ id: "tf", label: "tulipfarm.slack.com" }, { id: "acme", label: "acme.slack.com" }],
      account: "tf",
    },
    { id: "hubspot", label: "HubSpot", icon: <BrandIcon brand="hubspot" size="inline" />, connected: false },
  ]}
  onConnectIntegration={(integration) => connect(integration.id)}
  onIntegrationAccountChange={(integration, accountId) => useAccount(integration.id, accountId)}
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>value</code> is a Tiptap JSON document. Tags are
      <code>chatReference</code> nodes with <code>kind</code>, <code>id</code>, and
      <code>label</code>. A trigger is on only when its source is set. A source may return a promise. Leave out a menu
      or picker and its button goes away. Give a mode a <code>color</code> (any CSS color) to tint the box border, the
      mode chip, and its menu icon while that mode is on.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>integrations</code> turns app names in the text into chips with their icon, such as Slack or ChatGPT. Give
      one a <code>match</code> list for aliases, a <code>color</code> tint, or <code>connected: false</code> to mute it
      with a broken-link mark and offer <code>onConnectIntegration</code>. Set <code>account</code> to show which
      account an app uses in its tooltip. With two or more <code>accounts</code> and
      <code>onIntegrationAccountChange</code>, the tooltip's Switch button opens a menu to pick another; return a
      promise to show a spinner until the switch finishes. The text stays plain; call
      <code>findKeywords(value, integrations)</code> from <code>@tulipfarm/sprout/rich-text-editor</code> to know which
      apps a message uses. See the Rich Text Editor's keywords for matching rules.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Keyboard</h2>
    <p>
      <kbd>Enter</kbd> sends and <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> adds a line. In the panel, <kbd>↓</kbd> and{' '}
      <kbd>↑</kbd> move, <kbd>Enter</kbd> or
      <kbd>Tab</kbd> adds, and <kbd>Escape</kbd> closes. <kbd>⌘B</kbd> is bold,
      <kbd>⌘I</kbd> is italic, and <kbd>⌘K</kbd> turns a selected URL or email into a link, or removes a link.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
